<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
  Hand-written miniature OSM extract used by pipelines/tests/test_osm_routes.py.

  It is NOT downloaded. It exists to pin national-scale ingestion behaviour that
  the real national extract exercises (data/build/osm/ph.osm.pbf) but that the
  other fixtures cannot: route-id collisions, the skip-reason breakdown and the
  reader's national counters. Like the NCR fixture it carries dangling relation
  members (the bbox clip can leave them) plus one detached geometry fragment.

  Nodes (stops carry names; the rest are geometry only):
    5101 Alpha    (14.1000, 121.1000)  5102 Beta      (14.1050, 121.1050)
    5103 Gamma    (14.1100, 121.1100)
    5201 Delta    (14.2000, 121.2000)  5202 Epsilon   (14.2050, 121.2050)
    5203 Zeta     (14.2100, 121.2100)
    5301 Shared One (14.3000, 121.3000)  5302 Shared Two (14.3050, 121.3050)
    5401/5402      landmark geometry for ferry 7040
    5501/5502      landmark geometry for ferry 7041
    5601/5602      main fragment of route 7090
    5701/5702      DETACHED fragment of route 7090
    5801/5802      geometry of bus route 7004
    5851/5852      geometry of ferry 7010
    5901/5902      geometry of the nameless route 7070 and route 7080

  Ways:
    6101  5101,5102,5103     6201  5201,5202,5203     6301  5301,5302
    6401  5401,5402          6501  5501,5502          6601  5601,5602
    6602  5701,5702          6701  5801,5802          6751  5851,5852
    6801  5901,5902

  Relations (file order is ascending OSM id, as in a real extract):
    7001  route=bus, ref=7, "Route 7 North"
          -> bus-7 (first, lowest id: keeps the bare id)
    7002  route=bus, ref=7, "Route 7 South"
          -> bus-7-osm7002 (collision, a different corridor: no shared stops)
    7004  route=bus, ref=7, "Route 7 East"
          -> bus-7-osm7004 (collision)
    7010  route=ferry, ref=7 -> ferry-7: the same slug in another family does not collide
    7020  route=bus, ref=SHARED, stops 5301/5302 -> bus-shared
    7030  route=bus, ref=OTHER,  stops 5301/5302 -> bus-other: shares its member stop
          nodes with 7020; R16 keeps the stop ids route-namespaced
    7031/7032  route=bus, ref=ORDER, distinct corridors. 7032 is written first
          on purpose: ids are assigned by lowest OSM id, so 7031 keeps bus-order
          and 7032 becomes bus-order-osm7032 (file order must not decide)
    7040  route=ferry, name="Guadalupe - Pasig Ferry", no stop members
          -> ferry-guadalupepasig, two synthesized landmark stops
    7041  route=ferry, same name and same absent stops as 7040
          -> ferry-guadalupepasig-osm7041 (collision) and its own landmark stops
    7050  route=bus, ref=DANGLE, "Dangling Route": way 8999, nodes 9998/9999 and
          relation 7001 are all dangling/nested -> yielded with no geometry and
          four skipped members (1 dangling way, 2 dangling stop nodes, 1 nested relation)
    7060  route=road -> ignored: not a public-transport mode (counted)
    7070  route=bus with no name and no ref -> skipped and counted (no label)
    7080  route=bus, name="日本語" -> the slug is empty, so the id falls back to
          bus-osm7080 and the relation is still yielded (counted)
    7090  route=bus, ref=FRAG, "Fragmented": ways 6601 + 6602 are disconnected,
          so one detached fragment is dropped and counted
    7110-7113  route=bus, ref=REV: R19 reversal-aware collision group.
          7110 "North End" -> "South End" keeps bus-rev.
          7111 " south-end " -> "NORTH end" is the exact reverse: DROPPED and
               counted (routes_skipped_duplicate_direction).
          7112 the same direction as 7110: renamed bus-rev-osm7112.
          7113 has no from/to tags (not comparable): renamed bus-rev-osm7113.
    7100  type=boundary -> not a route relation; still counted as read
-->
